&lt;p>&lt;strong>Part 27 of the &lt;em>Learning Quantum Physics&lt;/em> series.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>An operator takes the column of a state and returns a new column. On one qubit the column has two entries, so the operator is a 2 by 2 matrix. Write the matrix on the left. Write the column on the right. Multiply.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;a href="https://dasarpai.github.io/dsblog/from-geometry-to-quantum-mechanics">From Geometry to Quantum Mechanics&lt;/a> uses these names side by side with arrows in a plane. This article defines each operator, writes its matrix, and says what the matrix does.&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>